  "bug_discussion": "Official fixing record: https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/10453\n\nFix a bug where arrays of GC refs were misreporting their count of GC edges (#10453)\n\n* Fix a bug where arrays of GC refs were misreporting their count of GC edges\n\nThey were accidentally reporting the size of their GC reference elements, rather\nthan the count.\n\n* fix miri ignore attr\n\nPreliminary source observation: The March 17 DRC change stored array byte size as GC edge count. Its March 21 fix stores array length instead. Upstream test paints the heap with a poison value, then creates a guest GC-ref array and collects it; the test says the old behavior panicked while tracing past the GC heap.\nSecurity impact, input reachability, earliest effective fix, and a three-revision oracle require independent review.",
